# ── pam_reattach — Touch ID for sudo inside tmux/screen (2026-08-24) ──────────
# Aaron 2026-08-24: "we need to add this to our ace package manager dependency
# tracking and make sure it's part of our declarative setup ... then i can run
# the 2nd part, that one liner is simple enough for a vibe coder."
#
# This row exists to DELETE a hand-typed command. tools/setup/touchid-sudo.ts
# used to tell the operator to run `brew install pam-reattach` themselves, which
# is precisely the manual step a declarative setup is for. The verifier now
# treats this row as the expectation and goes RED when the formula is declared
# here and absent on the host, so the declaration is CHECKED rather than hoped
# for (touchid-sudo-config.ts, `reattachDeclared`).
#
# WHAT IT DOES. Without it, sudo's Touch ID prompt cannot appear inside tmux or
# screen: the multiplexer's session is not the user's Aqua GUI session, so
# pam_tid has nothing to draw on and silently falls back to the password.
# pam_reattach re-attaches the process to that GUI session first, which is why
# touchid-sudo.ts emits it BEFORE pam_tid in /etc/pam.d/sudo_local. MEASURED
# ABSENT on the maintainer's host 2026-08-24 (no .so at either Homebrew prefix)
# while pam_tid was configured -- so Touch ID sudo was already inert in the
# shell agent work actually runs in, and nothing said so.
#
# Verified against the Homebrew API 2026-08-24, not from memory:
#   https://formulae.brew.sh/api/formula/pam-reattach.json
#   name pam-reattach | tap homebrew/core | version 1.3 | license MIT
#   upstream https://github.com/fabianishere/pam_reattach | dependencies: []
#   bottled arm64_tahoe/sequoia/sonoma/ventura/monterey/big_sur + x86_64
# Installs the module at <brew --prefix>/lib/pam/pam_reattach.so. touchid-sudo.ts
# PROBES both /opt/homebrew and /usr/local rather than assuming a prefix, and
# reads the Mach-O header to check the slice matches the host arch -- an
# x86_64-only module on an Apple Silicon Mac is present and unloadable.
#
# NOT tier-tagged (so: slim, every host), deliberately. It is a single ~50 KB
# bottled module with no dependencies, and the hosts most likely to be tiered
# down are exactly the headless/CI ones where a silent password fallback is
# hardest to notice. A tier= token here would buy no measurable disk and would
# make macos-install-sh-test skip the row.
#
# macOS-ONLY BY NATURE, and it is NOT mirrored into manifests/apt or
# manifests/windows. PAM-module-for-Aqua has no Linux or Windows meaning; a row
# that silently no-ops on another OS is a declaration that constrains nothing --
# the vacuity class wearing a manifest's clothes. The asymmetry is the honest
# record, the same way the YubiKey block above is deliberately shorter than apt's.
pam-reattach  # PAM module: re-attach to the Aqua session so Touch ID sudo works in tmux/screen

# ── Native C/C++ compile deps (Feldera-from-sources README + rustc crates) ────
# Symmetric with the apt block of the same name. Feldera's macOS brew line is
# `cmake openssl cyrus-sasl zlib zstd go pkg-config graphviz openjdk@21 maven
# python@3.10 oven-sh/bun/bun node@20`. We take the native-compile subset and
# refuse the SQL-compiler / Kafka / fips extras (go, graphviz, openjdk, maven,
# librdkafka). bun/node/python already come from mise. clang comes from
# `xcode-select`. zstd was apt-only until this row (ollama .tar.zst on Linux).
cmake
pkgconf         # Homebrew renamed pkg-config -> pkgconf; `brew list --formula` reports pkgconf, so the manifest must too
openssl@3       # headers+lib; keg-only. bare `openssl` is an alias; the installed keg is openssl@3, which is what `brew list --formula` reports
cyrus-sasl      # brew name for apt libsasl2-dev
zlib            # keg-only; macOS already ships zlib, formula matches the README
zstd            # headers+binary; apt already had the binary for ollama .tar.zst
